## 1. Mission Δv Budget (Earth Surface → Mars Surface)

| Mission Segment | Δv Required | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Earth surface → LEO (conventional) | 9.4 km/s | Includes ~1.5 km/s gravity loss, 0.2 km/s drag |
| **Earth surface → LEO (BGKPJR-VG)** | **6.1 km/s** | Tunnel+membrane provides 2.0 km/s; chemical provides rest |
| LEO → Trans-Mars Injection (TMI) | 3.6 km/s | Hohmann transfer, typical launch window |
| Mars orbit insertion (aerobraking) | 0.5 km/s | vs 2.1 km/s propulsive; aerobraking saves 1.6 km/s |
| Mars descent & landing | 0.8 km/s | Parachute + retropropulsive (supersonic retropropulsion) |
| **Total surface-to-surface** | **11.0 km/s** | vs **14.3 km/s** conventional |

**Δv savings from BGKPJR-VG over conventional: 3.3 km/s (23%)**

That 23% compounds exponentially in the rocket equation — final payload fraction improves by roughly **2.4×**.

