## 7. Honest Answer to Your Question

> "Mars Transfer as far as the payload that is another equation that needs to be figured into the equation to find the Maximum safe weight of Payload and Tare weight combined and if it can be manned mission or robot due to G-Force"

**Manned Mars mission is viable.** A 37 km tunnel at 4g is within the physiological envelope of lightly-trained astronauts — comparable to Soyuz ascent, easier than Shuttle. The horizontal g-force direction (eyeballs-back) is the most tolerable axis for humans.

**Maximum safe payload + tare for 500 t vehicle at 4g:**
- To LEO: 97.5 t (of which ~35 t is usable payload after vehicle structure)
- To Mars surface: 135 t (of which ~35 t is usable crew + supplies after life-support & return-fuel structure)

**To scale up to Starship-class delivery (130 t to Mars), wet mass grows to 1,500 t** — still within maglev thrust capability but requires stronger rails and higher-power coil banks.

**If you accept robot-only:** 10g tunnel drops to 14.5 km, costs 60% less, delivers 95+ t per flight to Mars. Strongly recommend building this first as a cargo line even before the crewed tunnel is operational.

